{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Niko1221/Strata/pulls/203","id":4686928674,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUpvcvc8AAAABF1zbIg","html_url":"https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/pull/203","diff_url":"https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/pull/203.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/pull/203.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Niko1221/Strata/issues/203","number":203,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"serve: prompt checkpoints copied out asynchronously (pinned staging on the prompt stream + a thread)","user":{"login":"q8atnight","id":229373104,"node_id":"U_kgDODav0sA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229373104?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/q8atnight","html_url":"https://github.com/q8atnight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/q8atnight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/q8atnight/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/q8atnight/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/q8atnight/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/q8atnight/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/q8atnight/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/q8atnight/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/q8atnight/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/q8atnight/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nA mid-prompt checkpoint (every `--prompt-cache-every` tokens, default 16K) currently stops the GPU:\n`cudaDeviceSynchronize()` plus pageable `cudaMemcpy`s into fresh vectors - ~370 ms of GPU idle per checkpoint on\nour box. This copies the same bytes out asynchronously: the running state goes to a pinned staging buffer through\nstream-ordered `cudaMemcpyAsync`s on the prompt stream (ordered after the chunk that produced the state, before\nthe next chunk overwrites it; ~10 ms of copy engine), and a thread moves it into the checkpoint's own vectors\nwhile the next chunk runs. The checkpoint joins `checks` at the next checkpoint, at a turn/root checkpoint, or\nonce the prompt is read. One commit on top of 0.1.27 (a790805).\n\n## Measured\n\n2x RTX 3090, IQ3_S, developed in the 0.1.24 + dual-GPU engine: the synchronous copy-out held the GPU idle\n~370 ms per mid-prompt checkpoint; async it overlaps the next chunk, so the prompt path does not wait for it.\nWith `--prompt-cache-every 16384` a 128K prompt takes ~7 checkpoints, so up to ~2.6 s of GPU idle (7 x ~370 ms, arithmetic, not separately measured).\n\n## Correctness\n\nThe checkpoint contents are unchanged - the same bytes, only copied later. The copy is stream-ordered between the\nchunk that wrote the running state and the chunk that overwrites it, so no sync is needed on the prompt path.\nA layer split keeps upstream's path untouched: its checkpoints are assembled from the stages' own parts, saved on\ntheir own streams, and a per-stage pinned staging does not obviously fit there - say so if you want it extended.\n\n## Switch\n\n`STRATA_CK_SYNC=1` = the old synchronous path. `STRATA_PREFILL_TIMING=1` traces the staging allocation and the\nenqueue time of each async checkpoint.\n","created_at":"2026-09-30T06:47:43Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T11:31:12Z","closed_at":"2026-09-30T11:31:12Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"8d1384b0b557b0aed2cfec48eb0866665aa1d42f","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Niko1221/Strata/pulls/203/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Niko1221/Strata/pulls/203/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Niko1221/Strata/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Niko1221/Strata/issues/203/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Niko1221/Strata/statuses/3b6100c101fbcee6612144854991a51eb1eb481b",